'x_mo-definition'('x_ZFA--0000658',"&quot;Epibranchials are dorsal parts of the gill arches.  Epibranchials 1-4 ossify in the epibranchial cartilages in a posterior to anterior progression.  The cartilaginous tips of the epibranchials articulate laterally with the cartilaginous tips of the ceratobranchials. Gill rakers are present on the anterior and posterior edges of epibranchials 2 4 and the posterior edge of epibranchial 1. A reduced gill raker is present on the anterior margin of epibranchial 1 in some specimens.&quot; [ZFIN:curator]") :- x_cid(a65b125bf37d4a).
