'x_mo-definition'('x_ZFA--0000316',"&quot;The basihyal is the 'tongue' of the a fish, the median and anteriorly projecting element of the ventral hyoid arch.Ossification of the cartilaginous basihyal is first visible at the posterior end of the club-shaped basihyal cartilage (6.0 mm). Ossification spreads throughout the cartilage, except for the anterior tip, which remains cartilaginous. The posteroventral tip extends between the left and right dorsal hypohyals.&quot; [ZFIN:curator]") :- x_cid(a65b125bf38068).
