'x_mo-definition'('x_ZFA--0001250',"&quot;Pharyngobranchial 2 (misidentified as pharyngobranchial 1 in Cubbage and Mabee, 1993 and Mayden 1989) is present and separate from pharyngobranchial 3.  It (8.0 mm) ossifies after pharyngobranchial 3. In the adult, the cartilaginous anterior end of the ossified pharyngobranchial 2 articulates with the cartilaginous medial tip of epibranchial 1. It articulates anterolaterally and posterolaterally with the anterior and posterior cartilaginous tips of epibranchial2.  In Cyprinidae pb3 overlaps pb2 (Siebert, 1987; Cavender &amp; Coburn, 1992) but does not fuse to it.&quot; [ZFIN:curator]") :- x_cid(a65b125bf38690).
