'x_mo-definition'('x_ZFA--0001239',"&quot;Ceratobranchial 5 ossifies before ceratobranchials 1-4.  In the adult, ceratobranchial 5 is heavily ossified and crescent-shaped with two to three rows of posteromedially directed teeth. The anteroventral tips of ceratobranchials 5 meet medially and are ligamentously joined.&quot; [ZFIN:curator]") :- x_cid(a65b125bf387a9).
