'x_mo-definition'('x_ZFA--0000621',"&quot;The quadrate is the dorsal bone in the jaw joint with the anguloarticular of the lower jaw.  Ossification of the quadrate, a cartilage bone, begins as a posteriorly projecting membranous spine between the symplectic cartilage and the preopercle (5.1 mm NL). The body of the quadrate ossifies first at the ball-and-socket articulation with the anguloarticular (6.5 mm). The adult quadrate is shaped roughly like an inverted triangle with a long, posteriorly projecting spine off its posteroventral edge.  The presence of a posteroventral or posterior process of the quadrate is a synapomorphy of Teleostei.&quot; [ZFIN:curator]") :- x_cid(a65b125bf3952b).
